{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"OESA-2026-4634","published":"2026-10-29T09:03:50Z","modified":"2026-10-29T09:15:41.110110884Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-14330","CVE-2026-5674"],"summary":"pipewire security update","details":"is a server and user space API to deal with multimedia pipelines,contains command line utilities.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nMultiple unbounded alloca() calls in the PulseAudio protocol server.(CVE-2026-14330)\n\nA flaw was found in PipeWire, a multimedia server. This vulnerability allows an attacker to escape sandboxed applications, such as Flatpak, by exploiting PipeWire&apos;s PulseAudio compatibility layer. An attacker with minimal permissions within a sandboxed environment can load a malicious library, leading to arbitrary code execution outside the sandbox and potential compromise of the user&apos;s system.(CVE-2026-5674)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"pipewire","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP1","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/pipewire&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["pipewire-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-alsa-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-debuginfo-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-debugsource-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-devel-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-gstreamer-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-help-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-libs-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm","pipewire-utils-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["pipewire-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["pipewire-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-alsa-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-debuginfo-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-debugsource-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-devel-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-gstreamer-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-help-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_64.rpm","pipewire-libs-0.3.63-7.oe2403sp1.x86_